# UI runtime error memory — opt-in only

Do **not** open, read, or consult `docs/ui/memory/ui-runtime-errors.md` by default.

Only read or update that file when the user **explicitly** instructs you to, for example:

- They `@`-mention the file or ask you to check/consult/update it
- They ask you to fix and document a UI runtime bug (use the `ui-runtime-bug-fix` skill)
- A task document they gave you explicitly says to read it for that task

Otherwise, skip it — even when working on Flutter UI, design-system components, or web-to-Flutter ports.
